The [[☃ definition 2]] will pass through points $(0,f(0))$ and $(6,f(6))$.

$\begin{align}
\text{slope}&=\dfrac{\text{change in }y}{\text{change in }x}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{f(6)-f(0)}{6-0}
\end{align}$

![Function f is graphed. The x-axis goes from negative 1 to 7. The graph is a curve. The curve starts in quadrant 2, moves upward with decreasing steepness, through a point at (0, f of 0) and (6, f of 6) and ends in quadrant 1. A secant line connects the 2 points.](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/6cd0f9a42438ae37ba19befb47e123514fff6f77)

We will need to know the values of $f(0)$ and $f(6)$ to find the slope.

$\begin{align}
f(0)&=\sqrt{4(0)+1}
\\\\
&=\sqrt{1}
\\\\
&=1
\\\\
f(6)&=\sqrt{4(6)+1}
\\\\
&=\sqrt{25}
\\\\
&=5
\end{align}$

Now we can find the slope:

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{f(6)-f(0)}{6-0}&=\dfrac{5-1}{6}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{2}{3}
\end{align}$
